mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East must double here. With only 5 pretty bad spades, definitely should not bid 4@S. Double is not pure penalty. Doubles in competition at the 4 level are ^*BValue Showing^*n. So double here says East has a better than minimum opening hand. |
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It asks partner to ^*BDo Something Intelligent^*n. Lots of times that will be a pass. But sometimes partner might bid a long suit of their own. Here pass is probably best by West, particularly at this vulnerability.|
PG| ***** 5 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|At this vulnerability I like pass by West better.|
